.Dd July 27, 2026
.Dt SECUREDMARC-CHECK 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm securedmarc-check
.Nd command-line DMARC policy evaluation tool
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl -from Ar domain
.Op Fl -mailfrom Ar domain
.Op Fl -spf Ar result
.Op Fl -dkim Ar domain
.Op Fl -dkim-result Ar result
.Op Fl -psl Ar file
.Op Fl n Ar nameserver
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Fl m Ar ms
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
evaluates DMARC for a set of already-authenticated identifiers and prints
the outcome as
.Dq key=value
lines on standard output.
It calls the same policy, DNS tree-walk, alignment, and disposition
functions
.Xr securedmarc 8
calls, so a result from
.Nm
is a statement about the shipped evaluator rather than about a separate
implementation written to pass tests.
.Pp
Unlike
.Xr securearc-check 8
and
.Xr securedkim-check 8 ,
.Nm
does not parse a message file.
Its inputs are the SPF and DKIM identifiers and results the milter chain
would have already placed in Authentication-Results headers by the time
.Xr securedmarc 8
runs, so they are given directly on the command line.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl -from Ar domain
Author Domain
.Pq RFC5322.From .
Required.
.It Fl -mailfrom Ar domain
RFC5321.MailFrom domain, the SPF identifier.
.It Fl -spf Ar result
SPF result:
.Dq pass , Dq fail , Dq none ,
etc.
Default:
.Dq none .
.It Fl -dkim Ar domain
DKIM Authenticated Identifier, the signature's
.Cm d=
value.
.It Fl -dkim-result Ar result
DKIM result:
.Dq pass , Dq fail , Dq none ,
etc.
Default:
.Dq none .
.It Fl -psl Ar file
Public Suffix List file, used only to veto a DNS tree-walk result, exactly as
the deprecated
.Cm PublicSuffixList
option in
.Xr securedmarc 8
does.
.It Fl n Ar nameserver
DNS nameserver IP address.
Default:
.Dq 127.0.0.1 .
.It Fl p Ar port
DNS nameserver port.
Default: 53.
.It Fl m Ar ms
Wall-clock budget for the evaluation, in milliseconds.
Default: 20000, matching the daemon's
.Cm MaxEvaluationMs .
0 disables the limit.
.It Fl h
Display usage information.
.El
.Sh OUTPUT
.Bl -tag -width "policy_domain" -compact
.It Cm result
DMARC result:
.Dq pass , Dq fail , Dq none , Dq temperror ,
or
.Dq permerror .
.It Cm disposition
Policy to apply:
.Dq none , Dq quarantine ,
or
.Dq reject .
.It Cm policy_domain
Name whose DMARC record supplied the policy.
.It Cm from_org
Organizational Domain of the Author Domain.
.It Cm spf_org
Organizational Domain of the SPF identifier, if walked.
.It Cm spf_aligned
.Dq yes
or
.Dq no .
.It Cm dkim_org
Organizational Domain of the DKIM identifier, if walked.
.It Cm dkim_aligned
.Dq yes
or
.Dq no .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It 0
A verdict was reached and printed to standard output, including
.Dq fail .
.It 2
The tool could not run:
.Fl -from
was not given, an option was invalid, or the Public Suffix List file could
not be loaded.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Evaluate a message that passed both SPF and DKIM, aligned:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securedmarc-check --from example.com --mailfrom example.com --spf pass \e
    --dkim example.com --dkim-result pass
.Ed
.Pp
Evaluate a message with only DKIM alignment, against a conformance suite's
own zone:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securedmarc-check --from example.com --dkim example.com --dkim-result pass \e
    -n 127.0.0.1 -p 5353
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr securedmarc 8 ,
.Xr securespf 8 ,
.Xr securedkim 8
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%T Domain-based Message Authentication, Reporting, and Conformance (DMARC)
.%R RFC 7489
.Re
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Daniel Morante
